    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The research plan commits to a Hold stance, and the evidence supports this balanced conclusion. The bull case is structurally sound \u2014 AAPL is up 22.4% over 60 days, sits 11% above the 50 SMA and 13.7% above the 200 SMA in a golden-cross regime, with exceptional $62.6B six-month operating cash flow and aggressive buybacks. However, the bear's timing argument is compelling: MACD histogram contracted 75% in four days, the stock closed below the 10 EMA for the first time since the rally began, and the highest-volume day (241.8M shares, 3.3x average) came on a down day. Critically, sentiment, macro, and income statement data are all UNAVAILABLE in this historical window, so there is no fundamental or sentiment confirmation to justify chasing at $205.53. The prudent action is to maintain the position at neutral weight without adding, respecting the technical warning signs while not exiting a confirmed uptrend. I will not initiate new longs at current levels and will respect the $198 stop level below the Bollinger middle band.\n\n**Entry Price**: 198.0\n\n**Stop Loss**: 198.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain existing position at or below neutral benchmark weight; do not scale up.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
